    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$B$ from $A$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$050^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "Since $AC=BC$, the base angles are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\angle CAB&=\\frac{180^{\\circ}-80^{\\circ}}{2}\\\\\n&=50^{\\circ}\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\angle ABC=50^{\\circ}$. The angle from north at $A$ to $AB$ is also $50^{\\circ}$ (alternate angles on parallel north lines). The bearing is $050^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$C$ from $A$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$100^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "The north lines are parallel, so the angle clockwise from north at $A$ to $AC$ and the $80^{\\circ}$ angle at $C$ are cointerior angles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Bearing of }C\\text{ from }A&=180^{\\circ}-80^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=100^{\\circ}\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q15-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$A$ from $B$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$230^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "Since $AC=BC$, $\\angle ABC=(180^{\\circ}-80^{\\circ})\\div2=50^{\\circ}$. The angle anticlockwise from north at $B$ to $BA$ is $180^{\\circ}-50^{\\circ}=130^{\\circ}$ (angles on a straight line).\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Bearing of }A\\text{ from }B&=360^{\\circ}-130^{\\circ}\\\\\n&=230^{\\circ}\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ],
